Targets: wasm
Releases: 9.2.9-
Subject: Skip the "do not run as root" check in the WebAssembly build
Purpose: PostgreSQL refuses to start as root (geteuid() == 0) to protect the host. Emscripten reports user 0 to every program, whether it runs in a browser or under node in a build container, and there is no host account to protect: the module runs inside the sandbox of its host. The check is skipped only when __EMSCRIPTEN__ is defined. 9.2.9 added the variable do_check_root to main() (the root check is skipped for --describe-config and -C), so the lines around this hunk of main.c are different; this variant is for 9.2.9 and later, the sibling without it for the earlier releases.
Components: src/backend/main/main.c, src/bin/initdb/initdb.c
Checks: postgres --version and postgres --single run under node as root (scripts/test-wasm-node.sh); initdb creates the template data directory as root (scripts/build-wasm.sh)
Origin: own

diff --git a/src/backend/main/main.c b/src/backend/main/main.c
--- a/src/backend/main/main.c
+++ b/src/backend/main/main.c
@@ -194,8 +194,11 @@
 	 * Make sure we are not running as root, unless it's safe for the selected
 	 * option.
 	 */
+#ifndef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+	/* (the WebAssembly host reports uid 0 to everyone and has no account to protect) */
 	if (do_check_root)
 		check_root(progname);
+#endif
 
 	/*
 	 * Dispatch to one of various subprograms depending on first argument.
diff --git a/src/bin/initdb/initdb.c b/src/bin/initdb/initdb.c
--- a/src/bin/initdb/initdb.c
+++ b/src/bin/initdb/initdb.c
@@ -551,6 +551,8 @@
 
 	struct passwd *pw;
 
+/* the WebAssembly host reports uid 0 to everyone and has no account to protect */
+#ifndef __EMSCRIPTEN__
 	if (geteuid() == 0)			/* 0 is root's uid */
 	{
 		fprintf(stderr,
@@ -561,8 +563,14 @@
 				progname);
 		exit(1);
 	}
+#endif
 
 	pw = getpwuid(geteuid());
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+	/* no account database in WebAssembly: the one user owns the data directory */
+	if (!pw)
+		return xstrdup("postgres");
+#endif
